        "Locally, the calendar is shaped by the monsoon and the festivals. The Ghaghra and the smaller rivers of the district can flood low land between July and September, which affects roads, electricity and sometimes schools. Dussehra and Diwali are family occasions with long breaks, and Chhath, widely observed across eastern Uttar Pradesh and Bihar, can pull a household out of routine for several days.",
