  faqs: [
    { question: "Is this page about Rudrapur in Uttar Pradesh or in Uttarakhand?", answer: "It is about Rudrapur in Deoria district, Uttar Pradesh. The much larger Rudrapur in Udham Singh Nagar, Uttarakhand, has its own page on this site. Lessons for either town run the same way, as live online one-to-one classes, so the practical difference is only in the local school context, the festival calendar and the cities nearby that a family compares." },
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Rudrapur, Deoria?", answer: "Send your child's IB programme, subject, level and exam session, and a shortlist comes back of tutors who teach that exact course. With no IB school in the district, matching is done nationally on syllabus fit, and the first lesson is a free trial so you can judge the teaching before paying." },
    { question: "Do you have IGCSE tutors for Rudrapur students?", answer: "Yes. Tutors teach Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel IGCSE content live online. We match on the syllabus code and tier your school or target school uses, such as Cambridge 0580 Extended Mathematics, rather than on a loose subject name, since the codes decide what is actually examined." },
    { question: "Do tutors come to my house in Rudrapur?", answer: "No. In-person home tuition is offered only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. In Rudrapur the lesson is private tuition from home, online: your child sits at a laptop with a camera and a whiteboard, and the tutor teaches live and one-to-one. It is the only format we offer for Deoria district." },
    { question: "What does IB or IGCSE tuition cost in Rudrapur?", answer: "The rate depends on programme, level, subject, session length and how many tutors can teach that exact course. Diploma HL Maths and sciences usually cost more than IGCSE Core subjects. We publish no fixed price list; your rate is quoted in writing before the free trial, and the tutor's location does not change it." },
    { question: "Which schools in Rudrapur offer IB or IGCSE?", answer: "We could not confirm any. Schools in Rudrapur and Deoria district follow the UP Board or CBSE. Families who want an IB or Cambridge school generally look at boarding options or at larger cities, and each school's current authorisation should be checked on the IB or Cambridge website before applying." },
    { question: "My child boards at an IB school elsewhere. Can a tutor help during holidays?", answer: "Yes, and it is one of the most common requests from small towns. We match a tutor to the boarding school's subject and level, and schedule lessons around its term dates, so that Dussehra, Diwali or summer breaks at home in Rudrapur are used for criterion feedback, past papers and the Internal Assessment." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial lesson?", answer: "Yes, every match begins with one. Your child works through a real topic from their own syllabus with the tutor, online and without payment. Afterwards you receive a short written plan, and you can accept it, ask for a different tutor, or stop without any obligation." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with my child's IB Internal Assessment?", answer: "A tutor can guide, but never write. That includes choosing a researchable question, reading the assessment criteria, planning data collection and giving feedback on drafts. The words, calculations and conclusions in any Internal Assessment, Extended Essay or TOK piece must be the student's own, which is also what the IB requires." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you cover for a Rudrapur family?", answer: "Both Maths courses at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, Computer Science, Psychology, Geography, History, English and Hindi are all covered. Language B and some less common subjects depend on tutor availability, so mention your exact combination in the first message." },
    { question: "Do you teach MYP and PYP, or only the Diploma?", answer: "All four programmes are covered. MYP work focuses on criterion-based tasks and the Personal Project, and PYP work on reading, writing and number confidence ahead of a move to a PYP school. Families in Rudrapur usually ask about these when a child is about to join a relative in a city." },
    { question: "Is online tuition as effective as in-person tuition for a Rudrapur student?", answer: "For IB and IGCSE it works well. A shared whiteboard, a camera on the student's handwriting and live marking of past papers give most of what a visit would, and a specialist tutor who is a thousand kilometres away is more useful than a general tutor down the lane. A steady internet connection is the main requirement." },
    { question: "How are tutors checked?", answer: "Before a tutor is introduced we look at qualifications, recent experience teaching the specific programme and subject, and familiarity with the assessment criteria. A trial lesson then shows how they actually teach. If the fit is wrong, we arrange another tutor without any awkwardness for the family." },
    { question: "When should my child start IB or IGCSE tuition?", answer: "Ideally at the start of the course: Class 9 for IGCSE, Class 11 for the Diploma. Starting early gives time to fix foundations before internal assessments and mocks. Students who join late, perhaps after a family move, can still catch up with a concentrated plan built around the first exam date." },
    { question: "My child is thinking of moving from the UP Board to IGCSE. Can you help?", answer: "Yes. A tutor can compare the two syllabuses for each subject, show where English writing and practical skills need strengthening, and help decide between Core and Extended tiers. The switch itself happens at a school elsewhere; we help the student become ready for it before and after." },
    { question: "Can lessons happen on weekends or late evenings?", answer: "Yes. Most Rudrapur families choose weekday evenings or weekend mornings. In May and June a morning slot before the heat avoids power-cut problems, and in winter an evening slot avoids foggy mornings. Slots can be changed with notice during festival weeks such as Chhath, Dussehra and Diwali." },
    { question: "What if we are not happy with the tutor?", answer: "Tell us, and we will arrange another tutor. Progress is reviewed every few weeks anyway, and a poor fit is treated as a matching problem, not a failure by the student. The written notes after each session make it easy to see whether something is really working." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected to any school or board?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service with no affiliation to the IB Organization, Cambridge, Pearson Edexcel, the UP Board, CBSE or any school in Rudrapur, Deoria or Gorakhpur. Names of boards and cities on this page are for context only and imply no endorsement." },
  ],

